A||||19||Gold-86SE||PMD needs your help (hypothetical)||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||10-13-2000||11:29 AM||||<BR>Here is your mission, if you so choose it.<P>PMD is recruiting ideas for a new production auto, slated for production no later than 2003/2004.  PMD has carefully studied the sales history of new-to-market autos from the Pontiac Division.  We have concluded that the Fiero was the most highly anticipated and highly sought after model ever produced my PMD.<P><BR>The parameters for this mission include the following, based on studies of the PMD Fiero. <P>1) The new model must be a two-seater, mid-engined vehicle.<P>2) Automatic and Standard transmissions will be available.<P>3) Engine combinations must meet the target market of commuters and introductory sports car themes.<P>4) The name Fiero must not, repeat, MUST NOT, be associated with this new design, due to lingering public doubt of the Fiero design.<P>5) Styling (Interior and Exterior) is open to your discretion.<P>6) Convience items must be part of the vehicle (such as: cup holders, additional power supplies for plug in equipement, no-hands cell phone design - is a major plus).<P>7) Designs must be plastic/fiberglass over space frame.<P>Additionallly, PMD wants sales 150,000 to 200,000 in the first year of production.<P>It is your mission to develop an offspring of the Fiero and bring that type of sales back to Pontiac.<P>This message will self-destruct in five seconds.<P>5...<P>4...<P>3...<P>2...<P>1...<P>Destruct.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.txconnect.com/home/rharris/signature-a.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||10-13-2000||11:03 PM||||<BR>Come on guys, no response.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||10-14-2000||10:47 AM||||If you want pics or cad drawings, this is a pretty tall request. Here are some ideas though...<P>1. The new car would be called "Pegasus", in order to appeal to the existing Fiero fans, but not frighten the uninformed detractors.<BR>It would be available in base, Formula, or GT trim levels<P>2. It would be based on a space frame similar to the existing design. Would have a suspension that is a logical evolution of the 88 design. Power steering would not be standard, but would be available.<BR>The design of the space frame would be changed in order to move the front wheelwells out of the passenger footwells, and to reduce the size of the center tunnel.<BR>The gas tank (16 gal.) would be located in the front compartment, which would be a bit larger, due to the redesign for the previously mentioned wheelhouse issue. It would be of a "fuel cell" design for safety during impacts. <P>3. GT and Formula versions of the car would be available with 17" "run-flat" tires, to eliminate the need for a spare tire.<P>4. Powertrains would include the current Sunfire 2.2 engine, the 3.5 V-6, or the 4.0 V-8, which are both currently available in the Aurora. <P>5. Transmissions would include a 5(or6) speed manual transaxle, or an automatic with overdrive.<BR> <BR>Anybody else?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-14-2000||11:29 AM||||Most of that makes allot of sence. Body wise I can't help but look at the Honda DelSol and see a slightly shrunk Fiero. Honda sold those things like candy.<P>moving the front wheels up would stretch the wheel base around a foot. maybe more. You'd end up with a shape along the lines of an old Datsun Z. You'd definatly have room for th fuel tank. Datsun/Nissan used to put an inline aluminum 6 in the space they had. <P>Having the fuel up there could cause some really squirly handling issues. 16 gallons is allot of weight. You could have handling that would chang dramatically as the fuel tank volume changes.<P>With the engine choices available it should run a 4 cyl that is already available with or without a turbo package. The biggest aluminum V6 available for the GT or Formula level, available with or without a supercharger.<P>Must have sunroof. <P>Power windows and Tilt steering should be standard. Especially if the cabin layout is anyhting close to original fiero. I can't get in or out without the wheel tipped up. There's no way to open/close the passengerside window from the driver's seat unless you unbelt and tip the wheel up to crawl over there.<P>improve cabin air exchange rate. Small cars get real stuffy real fast. I have windows and/or sunroof open nealry all year round. The design of the current roof allows it to be open in all but the heaviest rain.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gold-86SE||10-16-2000||02:34 PM||||<BR><B>Raydar</B>, wasn't looking so much for pics or drawings, but I do want to hear more of what Fiero owners would want or would like to see in a newly developed auto, if Pontiac decided to market a new mid-engine auto.<P>I like the name Pegasus, it has an exotic sound to it, and instills confidence much more than the name Fiero - just judging on the sound of the name here, not the product.<P>I could handle the trim packages, but instead of Base Coupe I would label it Sport Coupe and badge the car appropriately.  For example the rear decklid would be labeled "Sport Coupe"<P>Evolution of the 88 design, quite feasible.<P>Power steering - okay option, but agree with you - non-standard equipment.<P>I like the idea of moving the wheel wells forward to get them out of the cabin, but I wouldn't completely remove the wheel well. Instead move it to where it intrudes a few centimeters to only an inch or two.  I still desire a short wheelbase.<P>As for the gas tank - interesting thought.  However, instead locating it entirely in the front compartment, make the tank a T-shape that fits against the front of the car, just under the windshield and A pillars, but tuck the tank under the car in the tunnel to make it accomodate 16 gallons.<P>Cool thought about the run-flats and like the idea of the tranny/engine layouts.<P><BR><B>Ogre</B>, like the ideas of must haves: sunroof, tilt and power windows.<P>But like I stated earlier, I would prefer that the wheelbase not be extended too far, I personally don't car for the cigerette look that the 280/300 Z cars have.<P>If baffles were properly employed in the fuel tank and a T-shape fuel tank design used, balance and handling would not be compromised.<P><BR><B>Things I would like to see.</B><P>Short height popup lights, like those seen on some of the Z cars, where the lens is partially viewable even while turned off.<P>More luggage compacity through minor frame extension.<P>The tunnel.  I like the concept of being boxed in to the driver's seat, but I would like to see the height on of the tunnel made shorter.<P>I would like to see the shifter moved back away from the climate controls and radio pod, depending on the selected gear, one has to contort around the shifter to make adjustments will the controls.<P>I would also like to adjustable pedals and or seat to make for a more comfortable stretch for my legs.  Because if my right leg is comfortable on the gas and toe depress the clutch.<P>Opera window.<P>Flared fender wells on the GT.<P>The GT, should be optioned in Fastback and Notchback.<P>If the fuel tank is placed in the front compartment, move the fuel door to just in front of the windshield, driver's side of the car, located on top of the cowl.  The fuel door should have a gull-wing design that flips forward toward the headlights and has a lip that folds into the fender, so as to prevent fuel dribbles from damaging the paint.<P>Ragtop must be available.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||10-16-2000||03:51 PM||||does anyone remeber the old Raod runner? it was just a striped down car (dodge I think) nothing but engine tranny and brakes. That's what I think of what someone says formula. ya know? no power steering, no extra weight from power features (except the windows of course) and heavy sterio gear. Basically, have the formula trim be a striped down model w/ the alum v6 or 4.0 engine, leave everything as options tho. That way, you can cut the production cost down, and still have the fun power, which will draw in your young-mid age drivers who can't blow $30,000 on a car. The GT I think of more as a touring car, a little heavier, but with all the nice luxuries, for those of us who need to listen to CDs on 500 watt sterios while were driving  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I also like the idea of lengthening the car, just a bit tho, maybe like 6 inches. that should solve the leg room/tilt space that's my biggest complant, (my legs almost rub the stearing wheel) and move that shifter back from the controls and give us some drink holders!! <P>That 17" run flat idea is great, and with that extra 6" and lack of spare tire/jack, you could really get some extra storage room out of the front end.<P>a little bit more on the body curves would be nice, nothing too extreme, but have the back wheel wells flare a little more, and some sort of angle work on the hood.<P>and T-Tops or convertable should REALLY be an option. <P>thats about it for me.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick||10-16-2000||04:53 PM||||<BR>Geez, do you guys who desire more legroom in the Fiero play in the NBA or what? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I'm 6'3" and have absolutely no problem with the legroom (or headroom) in my '87.<P>I agree about the need for power windows though. Even with my long arms I can just barely wind up or down the passenger window from the driver's seat without dislocating my shoulder. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pontiaddict||10-16-2000||07:30 PM||||First, start off with an Opel Speedster.<BR>Stretch it out in all directions.<BR>Northstar anyone?<BR>6 speed or 4 speed auto<BR>Keep all the power doo-dads to a minimum.<BR>(Maybe optional)<BR>Redesign the weird looking body.<BR>Looking something like a Bonniville in front. (I like the look, but it needs to be more aerodynamic) And the 89 Fiero "Formula GT" styling in the back.(clear flying buttress = cool looks and good visisbility)<BR>Keep the fuel tank in the middle. (safe and well ballanced)<P>I would mangle some pictures together, but I need a better computer first.<P>It looks cool in my head, maybe it will fall out someday.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||10-16-2000||08:30 PM||||Patrick, It's not an issue of there being enough room to stretch out your legs. It's really about the way the wheelhouse intrudes nearly a foot into the footwell. It crowds your legs in towards the center. That's the biggest complaint that "she who must be obeyed" has, regarding my Fiero. <BR>(I used to find it annoying when I had a four speed GT. Don't mind it as much with the auto.)<P>I'd also like to see a targa roof option.  And fixed headlights. No moving parts. <P>As for body shape (I do expect a lot of...  uhh... discussion, here), I kind of like the basic shape of the current Trans Am, <I>except</I> for all the scoops and slots and crap on the front. And that Batmobile-looking spoiler. I like the "base" Firebird spoiler much better.<BR>And <I>please</I> no slats in the lower cladding, like the Grand Am has. I think all those ridges spoil the lines of an otherwise beautiful car. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||10-16-2000||10:11 PM||||how tall is "she" jeeze. I'm 6' and I can more than stretch comfortably on that side. I like the wheel wells where they are precicly because I can put my foot on it. (I wasn't saying increase the wheel base. Just what I thought it would look like if you went that far.<P>I wasn't even considering slosh in the tank. the weight alone would be a significant issue. Isn't gasoline something like 6-7 pound per gallon. Just on the conservative side, 6*16 is 96, 7*16=112. 100# changes focused close to an axle are pretty large. To use another example my pinto had an 11 gallon tank in the back. It's suspension was in good shape but you could feel the car drop at least an inch as you filled it from empty. Those leaf springs were pretty stiff.<P>Personally I don't want a car this small with a 16 gallon tank. Most small cars have small tanks. There's a whole bunch of reasons for it. Even my V8 73 Maverick only had a 11 gallon tank. Remember you are also getting better millage from todays engine & tranny compinations. You can go allot farther on the same gas now. It's not at all farfetched to think of putting a turbo diesle in one of these. (If you think turbo diesle is slow find one of the old VW rabbits that had it.)||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||10-16-2000||11:32 PM||||Ok.. Del Sol-styled body for the notchback, (not sure about the fastback..) with a bit of late model Firebird thrown in. (nose and rear end)<P>more smooth interior, not boxy.. definitely power windows and locks.. ABS should be an option, same with power steering.. I agree about the fixed headlights too. cup holders.. shifter further back, to leave more room for putting in a CD, changing the temp controls.. Sport Coupe should have a turbo 4cyl.. GT either a turbo 4cyl, turbo V6 or small V8.. and the Formula should have the option of a V6 or V8 (same as GT)<BR>one suggestion though.. skip the huge side banner for the Formula.. it looks very 80s.... I'd suggest also putting in airbags, as an option.. better cooling.. (decklid scoop?) and design the body so it looks sleeker than the 80s Fiero.. gotta be more laid back, like the Chop-top ones. move the battery up front, NEEDS A REAL GLOVEBOX.. A/C is standard.. something fancier (dual zone?) as an option.. AM/FM + casette standard, CD as an option.. definitely gotta have a sunroof or T-Tops.. and a frame around the doors, for better security! Tilt steering is also a must.. I do NOT fit in a Fiero without tilt and a sunroof...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>anyway, that's it for now.. hehe<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000011||RobertVol||10-17-2000||10:00 AM||||Since GM likes to intergrate their engines, I was thinking of maybe the 3.4 liter engine with that Eaton Supercharger, that motor trend had a couple of months ago in that article about the Grand AM. that would a logical fit. agree with the design option though. and a six speed. option. with that manual shifting automatic from the steering wheel!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||pollock||10-17-2000||12:25 PM||||in the spirit of the immortal Brother Bluto:<P>TARGA! TARGA! TARGA!<P>everybody!<P>TARGA! TARGA! TARGA!<P>I don't give a damn where you put the engine, as long as it's huge and the car's RWD.<P>Gotta have a stick with at least 5 gears.<P>Notchback version?  Gimme a break.  No thanks. <P>[This message has been edited by pollock (edited 10-17-2000).]<P>Wait a minute.... I just designed a Vette!<p>[This message has been edited by pollock (edited 10-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tigger||10-17-2000||12:42 PM||||I think we should wait a few more years...<P>Why? look what they came up with for the Aztek?  Think about it!  Instead of a targa top two seater we'd have one with a tent!<P>Besides, good things are worth waiting for anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000014||Formula||10-17-2000||09:49 PM||||<P>ok, my take on this....<P>same wheel base, I'm 6' with an auto and have no problems with the space, its actually more roomy then most sport trucks Ive been in.<P>Pegasus Formula<BR>the formula version should be complelty stripped except for stereo, heater, and tilt.  leave power windows out! also it will have the notchback styling (can you say 2000 lotus espirit), and a boxy, lightweight racing style interior (like a nascar), 2500 lbs!<P>Pegasus GT <BR>the GT version will be completly loaded with ps, pb, tilt, cruise, etc... it will come with the 2001 firebird ws-6 wheels (17" chrome 5 stars), optional leather, a smooth curvy interior like a new corvette, and it will have a fastback exterior (firebird front, smooth corvette "like" back, with the clear glass like archies kit car, with it totaling in at 3300 lbs.<P>Pegasus<BR>base model, only known as pegasus, will be a notchback (lotus espirit), with all of the gt's standards as options, but none of the gts options available, and will come with a little bit more refined interior then the formula (something like a sunfire). 2700 lbs<P>Pegasus Type-R<BR>this model will be the Cobra-R like model that will always be on motortrend covers so that base coupe sells go up! will have the GT exterior but be a formula inside and have special engine options. 1 year only<P>Pegasus GTS<BR>GT  with stripes, like later model ford probes. different gears, 1 year only<P>Pegasus INDY<BR>Formula used in 2004 indy race, will be white and grey with INDY on the sides. 1 year only<P>Pegasus SE<BR>Special Edition, will be a base coupe with the GT engine at the 5 year anniversary and to honor the demise of the corvette. will also have GT interior (more like a fancy formula) 1 year only<P>Drivetrain Options<BR>Formula <BR>N/A 3800, SC 3800<BR>5 speed manual (4.80 gears)<P>GT<BR>N/A 3800, SC3800<BR>4 speed auto, 5 speed manual (3.33 gears)<P>Base<BR>2.4 liter I4<BR>5 speed manual, 4 speed auto (3.33 gears)<P>Type R<BR>Z03 350, 383 hp<BR>6 speed manual (4.80 gears)<P>GTS<BR>SC 3800<BR>5 speed manual, 4 speed auto (4.10 gears)<P>INDY<BR>Z03 350 SC, 470 hp<BR>6 speed manual (4.80 gears)<P>SE<BR>N/A 3800, SC 3800, 2.4 liter I4<BR>4 speed auto, 5 speed manual (3.33 gears)<P>Pricing<BR>Formula<BR>$13,000-$17,000<P>GT<BR>$15,000-$23,000<P>Base<BR>$10,000-$15,000<P>Type R<BR>$30,000-$50,000<P>GTS<BR>$16,000-$24,000<P>INDY<BR>$40,000-$60,000<P>SE<BR>$10,000-$19,000<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||theogre||10-17-2000||11:12 PM||||even worrying about weight I want the power windows. I'd never consider a car this wide without them. The motors don't add noticable weight. I've hand carried both power and non powered doors recently.... you can't tell which is which they both weigh a ton. The power window door can't be more than 1.5-2 pounds heavier.<P>Not having them is a royal pain in the _____. First thing I do when I get in my car is open both windows unless it feezing cold or raining. There's no way in hell to reach the passengers side window from the drivers seat without a tool or unless you unbelt, tip the wheel up, have the car in park, and crawl 3 feet or more. these cars aren't tiny freaking hondas.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Pontiaddict||10-18-2000||07:45 PM||||Power windows aren't really an option anymore. They are standard on all but the cheapest of cars. Air bags will be standard due to government regs. I, myself, don't like AC, T-tops, or the fastback (keep them as options).<P>Formula, you're on the right track. here's a Few changes.<P>1: Using an aluminum frame can knock nearly half a ton off the weight<P>2: Change Pegasus Type-R to Pegasus GTP. Kill the GTS model.<P>3: New pace cars should have better paint schemes than the grey/white.<P>4: Carbon fiber body panels should be available for "High performance use" (Backdoor option)<P>5: Love the reasoning for the SE model, but make available longer than 1 year.<P>6: If the car is to survive, It needs LOTS of aftermarket support. Give preproduction models to performance equipment manufacturers for testing and to make show/Power Tour cars out of them.<P>7: I'm still not sure about the Pegasus name.<P>8: A 6 speed ought to be available eventually. Make any GM car's corporate engine fit the car. (New Impallas will get V8s soon so a transaxle will be available to fit.<P>9: While I'm dreaming, NOS is optional. Carbon fiber production somehow gets really cheap, so they made the entire chassis out of it. Still has dent resistant, removeable panels.<P>Man, this got big in a hurry! I'll leave it at that.||||reg||1
Z||000017||StuGood||10-19-2000||12:16 AM||||Details, details...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Put the door lock cylinders in the C pillar, so that it's easy to insert and operate the key.<P>Provide a small but useable trunk in front, improve radiator airflow, use run-flats and ditch the spare tire.  Leave (1988)gas tank as-is, but make the gas gage sender dead reliable.  Ditto for the headlight actuators.<P>Improve clutch linkage - cast iron hydraulic cylinders, greaseable bushings for clutch fork actuator shaft. <P>Relocate engine oil dipstick and starter to opposite side of engine.  Use stainless coolant crossover tube in front of engine.  <P>Standard engine: 3.1 V6<BR>1st Optional engine: 3800 V6<BR>2nd Optional engine: 3800SC V6<BR>           ||||reg||6
Z||000018||StuGood||10-19-2000||06:46 PM||||...5-speed manual transaxle is a must.  Automatic optional - but make it an autostick so even I can stand to drive it, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Bigger wheel/tire assemblies (standard) to fill out the rear wheel openings.  That, and/or shrink the wheel openings to suit.<P>More exterior colors/striping options.  Right, Fiero5?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">     ||||reg||3
Z||000019||WKDFIRO||10-19-2000||08:38 PM||||150,000 to 200,000 a year???????<P>PMD is smoking cheap crack if they want to make the same mistakes all over again! One of the problems with the Fiero is if it wanted to be a sports car, YOU CAN'T SELL A LOT OF THEM! <P>Corvettes don't sell many, hell, The Acura NSX is being sold at a loss to Honda with less than 2,000 a year. So you go back to the same problem originally. Is it a sports car or econo car? Econo car will sell but they already have the Grand Am selling very nicely. Sports car? If you make it the Firebird replacement you CAN'T have 100,000+! The bean counters will win every time!<P>WHY would you want to see your car at every street corner and stop light? Look how sick we are of all the Hondas!<P>GM has proven time and time again how they can completely mishandle the marketing of superior products. Case in point. Camaro/Firebirds - MORE powerful than Mustangs, MORE economical bang for the buck than mustangs, MORE stylish inside and out than Mustangs...<P>Then WHY have Mustangs been outselling the COMBINED numbers of Camaro/Firebirds??? <P>The mission was aborted before it even got off the ground. <P>PMD wants a new car, perhaps they need to get a rapid cranialrectalotomy (MY GOD what manner of hysterical mind altering chemicals is the AZTEC?)and make a Corvette fighter not just another Camaro twin.<P>Reality being what it is I would love to be proven wrong...please? <P>PMD, prove me wrong PLEASE!!!!||||reg||1
